Z||000000||86er||12-27-2001||11:10 PM||||My 86 V-6 oil pressure guage after warm up the needle begins to waver and drop close to the red zone. Any thoughts?<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-28-2001||12:06 AM||||What weight oil are you using?  Check the oil pressure sending unit, and make sure it is not leaking.  If it is either leaking at its connection on the block, near the oil filter, or at the base of the unit itself, you could be getting false readings from it.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierojoesig2.gif">  <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||JayLT1||12-28-2001||01:50 AM||||i have the exact same problem. HUH  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>86 Black GT (95LT1 on the way)||||reg||1
Z||000003||thomas_l||12-28-2001||05:34 AM||||Mine has 168k miles and loose bearings causing that (slight chatter over 3500 rpm). I used Castrol Syntec 5w-50 on the last oil change and it really helped quiet things down and keeps the oil pressure from nose diving when hot.||||reg||1
Z||000004||86er||12-28-2001||09:14 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 86er:<BR><B>My 86 V-6 oil pressure guage after warm up the needle begins to waver and drop close to the red zone. Any thoughts?<BR>Thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I am using 10-30 Mobil 1. I'll check for leaks, thanks. Maybe I'll change the sender.<BR>The wavering & low pressure only during idle.<p>[This message has been edited by 86er (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_24||12-28-2001||09:35 AM||||My 87Gt with a new 2.8 with 7 miles on it does the same thing.  I even have a new oil pressure sending unit on there.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
